  27:     splits the remaining cells into equal-width left and right regions on the
  28:     background. Reflected foreground overlaps, when present, have the same color.
  29: 
  30:     Rule
  31:     Remove the separator column, mirror the right region horizontally, and
  32:     overlay it onto the left region. For each output pixel, keep the foreground
  33:     color from whichever folded side is non-background; if both sides are
  34:     foreground, their colors must agree.
  35: 
  36:     Key insight
  37:     The two sides are complementary halves around the separator, and the output
  38:     is the separator-free left-side coordinate system after folding the right
  39:     side inward.
  40:     """
  41:     g = np.asarray(grid, dtype=int)
